<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herod Agrippa I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 11 BCE–44 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Agrippa I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herod Agrippa I was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a>, raised in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and a friend of the emperors <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caligula">Caligula</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>. Caligula gave him the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetrarchy">Tetrarchy</a> of Philip with the title of king in 37, and by 41 Claudius had added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judaea</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>, reuniting his grandfather's realm. He died suddenly at Caesarea in 44, and Judaea returned to direct Roman rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i.jpg" alt="Herod Agrippa I" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adaptation of CNG by Mogador · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Piece_Agrippa_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 41 Claudius gave it with the title king to Herod, brother of <b>Agrippa I</b>, now known as Herod of Chalcis.</blockquote><a href="/state/herodian-kingdom-of-chalcis">Herodian Kingdom of Chalcis</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Herod Agrippa I</b>, grandson of Herod the Great and friend of Caligula, received the former Tetrarchy of Philip with the title king in 37.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-herod-agrippa">Kingdom of Herod Agrippa</a></li><li><blockquote>Accused of conspiracy by his nephew <b>Agrippa</b>, he was deposed by Caligula in 39 and exiled to Gaul.</blockquote><a href="/state/tetrarchy-of-galilee-and-peraea">Tetrarchy of Galilee and Peraea</a></li><li><blockquote>In 37 Caligula granted it to <b>Herod Agrippa I</b>, making it the core of the Kingdom of Herod Agrippa.</blockquote><a href="/state/tetrarchy-of-philip">Tetrarchy of Philip</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Caesarea Maritima, in what is now <a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.5,34.89&amp;year=24" aria-label="Caesarea Maritima on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5446 982 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Herod Agrippa I"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5896 1252h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5896 1252h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=32.5,34.89&amp;year=24">What was here in 24 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
